The key is to keep track of the selector, the data array, and the output tape. When the selector is out of bounds, we assume the cell is 0. For `+` and `-` on an assumed cell, we just ignore the operation. For `*`, we add the ASCII value of the selected cell to the output tape. For `!`, we add a new cell with value 0 to the data array.

